<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#rajab">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajab</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajab is the seventh month of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar">Islamic lunar calendar</a>. It is one of the four sacred months in which fighting was traditionally forbidden, a custom inherited from pre-Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. Muslim tradition places the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>'s night journey and ascension (Isra and Mi'raj) in this month, and it has long been associated with voluntary fasting and devotion.</p></div>
